{"content":[{"c":["ABDI"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Member of the Merari clan of Levites. Abdi’s grandson Ethan was a musician in David’s time (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.44","r":"1Chr.6.44","rawR":"1Chr.6.44","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.44","value":"1Chr.6.44"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:44"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.15.17","r":"1Chr.15.17","rawR":"1Chr.15.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.15.17","value":"1Chr.15.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"15:17"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Levite whose son Kish served in Hezekiah’s time (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.29.12","r":"2Chr.29.12","rawR":"2Chr.29.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.29.12","value":"2Chr.29.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 29:12"},"). This Abdi has sometimes been confused with Abdi #1."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Member of the Elam clan in Ezra’s time. This Abdi is listed as one of the Israelites who married a foreign wife after the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.26","r":"Ezra.10.26","rawR":"Ezra.10.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.26","value":"Ezra.10.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:26"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Abdi","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:44","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.44","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.44","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.44"},{"anchorText":"15:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.15.17","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.15.17","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.15.17"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 29:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.29.12","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.29.12","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.29.12"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 10:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.10.26","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.10.26","sourceRefExact